<para id="RM000001X0Q00XX" category="C" type-id="800K2" name-id="066O6-00" from="200708">
<dtccode>P0617/43</dtccode>
<dtcname>Starter Circuit (High)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000001X0Q00XX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D9F00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The cranking hold control system energizes the starter until the engine control computer, which has detected the starter signal (STSW) from the main body ECU, determines that the engine has started. The engine control computer that receives the starter signal (STSW) outputs the ACC cut relay signal (ACCR) to the main body ECU to turn ON the ST CUT relay, preventing flickering of the meter, clock, audio, etc., and the engine control computer also outputs a signal to the STAR terminal. The STAR output signal turns ON the ST relay via the neutral start switch assembly to operate the starter. Also, while the engine is being cranked, the starter operation signal is also sent to the STA terminal of the engine control computer. The main body ECU monitors the terminal voltage on the output side of the ST CUT relay, and protects or drives the starter circuit if there is a malfunction.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A153079J02" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<ptxt>The DTC is detected when the starter operation signal (STA) is input to the engine control computer while the vehicle is being driven.</ptxt>
